00:02:33.500 --> 00:02:35.048
MARK MANDEL: How
can they contribute?

00:02:35.048 --> 00:02:37.400
MELODY MECKFESSEL:
[LAUGHS] Well, you

00:02:37.400 --> 00:02:40.760
know we talk a lot about
Google Cloud Platform being

00:02:40.760 --> 00:02:42.230
an open cloud.

00:02:42.230 --> 00:02:43.820
And so from a
developer-- you know,

00:02:43.820 --> 00:02:46.130
there's a platform aspect
of that, which means

00:02:46.130 --> 00:02:48.860
open APIs and open protocols.

00:02:48.860 --> 00:02:50.990
But there's a
developer and operator

00:02:50.990 --> 00:02:53.630
or human-centered
perspective on what

00:02:53.630 --> 00:02:55.340
it means to be an
open cloud, and that

00:02:55.340 --> 00:02:57.950
means having the
freedom to choose

00:02:57.950 --> 00:03:00.050
what makes you most productive.

00:03:00.050 --> 00:03:04.070
And I think about it in
kind of three aspects.

00:03:04.070 --> 00:03:05.870
From a tooling
perspective, for things

00:03:05.870 --> 00:03:09.090
that need to scale and
work well on the platform,

00:03:09.090 --> 00:03:10.850
they're going to be
GCP products and we

00:03:10.850 --> 00:03:12.770
have several that we're
announcing this week.

00:03:12.770 --> 00:03:14.600
Beyond that, open
source tooling.

00:03:14.600 --> 00:03:16.970
This is a direct way that
developers and operators can

00:03:16.970 --> 00:03:19.070
contribute, and we have
some great open source

00:03:19.070 --> 00:03:22.610
tools that we work on with
partners and other enterprise

00:03:22.610 --> 00:03:23.360
companies.

00:03:23.360 --> 00:03:25.520
And then the final
thing is partners.

00:03:25.520 --> 00:03:28.460
So developers and operators
working with partners,

00:03:28.460 --> 00:03:30.650
we want to make sure they
work well on the platform.

00:03:30.650 --> 00:03:35.570
So it's kind of this combination
of GCP tools, open source

00:03:35.570 --> 00:03:37.880
tools that developers
and operators contribute

00:03:37.880 --> 00:03:41.300
to, and then our partner
products that work really well.

00:03:41.300 --> 00:03:43.804
MELANIE WARRICK: Why do you
believe in an open cloud?

00:03:43.804 --> 00:03:45.720
MELODY MECKFESSEL: You
know, it's fascinating,

00:03:45.720 --> 00:03:48.920
but when you come
back to the humans,

00:03:48.920 --> 00:03:52.230
the developers and operators
that are using the cloud--

00:03:52.230 --> 00:03:55.220
we've done some research on this
topic around both productivity

00:03:55.220 --> 00:03:58.010
and kind of what's
happening in the ecosystem.

00:03:58.010 --> 00:04:00.860
65% of developers
we've surveyed say

00:04:00.860 --> 00:04:04.520
that they have freedom to choose
what makes them productive.

00:04:04.520 --> 00:04:05.840
So think about that.

00:04:05.840 --> 00:04:08.930
If the developers and
operators are choosing,

00:04:08.930 --> 00:04:12.890
that means that they have
autonomy and they have freedom

00:04:12.890 --> 00:04:14.580
and they have a voice.

00:04:14.580 --> 00:04:18.920
And so our job within GCP, and
specifically in DevOps tools,

00:04:18.920 --> 00:04:21.920
is to enable them to be
productive and maybe,

00:04:21.920 --> 00:04:24.320
you know, just a
little bit happy.

00:04:24.320 --> 00:04:27.205
As developers and operators,
we keep raising the bar, right?

00:04:27.205 --> 00:04:28.580
MELANIE WARRICK:
What, happiness,

00:04:28.580 --> 00:04:29.440
when you're developing?

00:04:29.440 --> 00:04:30.648
I didn't know that's a thing.

00:04:30.648 --> 00:04:32.520
MELODY MECKFESSEL: [LAUGHTER]

00:04:32.520 --> 00:04:36.440
MARK MANDEL: So what is Cloud
Build and what is Stackdriver?

00:04:36.440 --> 00:04:38.180
MELODY MECKFESSEL:
Great question.

00:04:38.180 --> 00:04:42.560
Cloud Build is a continuous
integration and delivery

00:04:42.560 --> 00:04:43.250
platform.

00:04:43.250 --> 00:04:46.200
It's a way to automate
the build and test.

00:04:46.200 --> 00:04:48.184
So once you have
your code written,

00:04:48.184 --> 00:04:49.850
this is a way to build
and test and make

00:04:49.850 --> 00:04:51.433
sure that you're
sending something out

00:04:51.433 --> 00:04:53.460
to your users
that's high quality.

00:04:53.460 --> 00:04:55.855
It includes things
like security baked in.

00:04:55.855 --> 00:04:58.640
We have vulnerability
scanning features

00:04:58.640 --> 00:05:01.190
to check and see if there's
any issues with the images

00:05:01.190 --> 00:05:02.480
that you're releasing.

00:05:02.480 --> 00:05:04.670
We contribute with
Netflix to something

00:05:04.670 --> 00:05:07.070
called Spinnaker, which
is part of Cloud Build.

00:05:07.070 --> 00:05:09.560
It's an open source
deployment platform.

00:05:09.560 --> 00:05:12.460
So it's just-- again, if
I come back to the humans,

00:05:12.460 --> 00:05:14.840
I want to get features
out to my users.

00:05:14.840 --> 00:05:17.010
I want to get them out
safely and securely,

00:05:17.010 --> 00:05:19.275
and I want to move as
fast as I possibly can.

00:05:19.275 --> 00:05:20.150
MARK MANDEL: Awesome.

00:05:20.150 --> 00:05:21.816
And these-- just in
general, these sort

00:05:21.816 --> 00:05:24.440
of continuous integration tools,
these tool aren't specifically

00:05:24.440 --> 00:05:26.648
container based, they can
be used in any Google Cloud

00:05:26.648 --> 00:05:27.650
Platform tooling?

00:05:27.650 --> 00:05:29.650
MELODY MECKFESSEL: Yeah,
we support most aspects

00:05:29.650 --> 00:05:33.980
of the Google Cloud Platform and
integrate well with Kubernetes.

00:05:33.980 --> 00:05:37.610
All you essentially have is
you can set up your cloud

00:05:37.610 --> 00:05:38.840
build and be good to go.

00:05:38.840 --> 00:05:40.670
You mentioned
Stackdriver, Melanie,

00:05:40.670 --> 00:05:42.330
I wanted to come back to that.

00:05:42.330 --> 00:05:45.290
So there's the build and
test and release aspect,

00:05:45.290 --> 00:05:47.690
but there's also once your
service is running on Google

00:05:47.690 --> 00:05:51.680
Cloud Platform, how do
you monitor and get alerts

00:05:51.680 --> 00:05:54.590
and understand what's
happening with the service

00:05:54.590 --> 00:05:57.800
through logging and features
like error reporting?

00:05:57.800 --> 00:06:00.860
So we are continuing
to evolve Stackdriver

00:06:00.860 --> 00:06:04.850
to be the set of products
which allow operators to move

00:06:04.850 --> 00:06:07.070
at the speed of Google SREs.

00:06:07.070 --> 00:06:09.230
